<ArchivePost
  title="Docker Compose Error"
  date="13 December 2019"
  tags="WordPress · Docker"
  description="Resolving an unsupported Docker Compose workdir API error."
  canonicalPath="/pensieve/docker-error/"
>
  <h2>Problem</h2>
  <p>
    While updating a project with webpack, I encountered a strange error when running a simple
    Composer script through Docker Compose.
  </p>
  <pre><code>#!/bin/bash
docker-compose exec -w /var/www/html/wp-content/themes/skela wordpress composer "$@"</code></pre>
  <p>Running <code>./bin/composer install</code> returned:</p>
  <pre><code>ERROR: Setting workdir for exec is not supported in API &lt; 1.35 (1.30)</code></pre>
  <p>The error was coming from the <code>-w</code> flag in the command.</p>

  <h2>Solution</h2>
  <p>
    Updating the Compose file version from <code>3.5</code> to <code>3.6</code> resolved the issue.
  </p>
  <pre><code>version: '3.6'
services:
  wordpress:
    build: .</code></pre>
</ArchivePost>
